Student: Chaplin Marchais
Date   : 11/14/26
Project: SMSH Project 5

Summary:
    This project contains smsh, a small interactive command shell. Build it
    with make and start it with ./smsh; it displays the > prompt, reads one
    command per line, and runs external programs using fork, execvp, and wait.

    Built-in commands and variable support include:
         NAME=value stores a shell variable; set lists stored variables
         export NAME adds a variable to child-process environments
         cd PATH changes the shell's working directory
         $NAME substitutes a variable when it is a complete argument

    The shell supports a simple if command, followed by then, a conditional
    command block, and fi. Commands are split on spaces and tabs; quoting,
    pipelines, and input/output redirection are not implemented.

Files:
    smsh.c        -- main loop, prompt, initialization, and signal setup
    process.c     -- command dispatch and external program execution
    process.h     -- command processing function declarations
    builtin.c     -- built-in commands, assignments, and variable substitution
    builtin.h     -- built-in command function declarations
    controlflow.c -- handling of if, then, fi, and conditional execution
    controlflow.h -- control-flow function declarations
    varlib.c      -- shell variable storage and environment management
    varlib.h      -- variable library function declarations
    splitline2.c  -- command-line reading, tokenization, and argument cleanup
    splitline2.h  -- command parsing function declarations
    flexstr2.c    -- dynamically growing string and string-list helpers
    flexstr2.h    -- flexible string and list structures and declarations
    smsh.h        -- shared shell declarations
    Makefile      -- builds smsh from the shell source files; make clean removes
                     object files and the executable
    Plan          -- design document for the project
